# Flywheel framework (managed block — edits outside the markers are yours, inside are flywheel's)

Project: (one line — what this project is; seed prompt fills this)

This adapter runs flywheel in **degraded mode** (no subagents — see
flywheel/ORCHESTRATION.md §8). Read `flywheel/INDEX.md` now; it indexes everything.

## Session protocol
1. Read `flywheel/STATUS.md` first — resume from it, don't re-derive.
2. Before ending / context low: run the wrapup procedure inline — update STATUS.md +
   `flywheel/state/*.json`, `bash flywheel/check.sh`, rebuild dashboard
   (`python3 flywheel/dashboard/build.py`), commit per `flywheel/GIT.md`.

## Degraded-mode tier rules
- To do tier work, paste the matching template from `flywheel/TEMPLATES.md` into THIS
  session and announce "operating as <tier>". Follow that tier's rules until the task
  reports back.
- Verification is never self-performed: verifier/auditor passes (Template 4) run in a
  FRESH session with clean context. Ask the human to start one (or queue it in
  `state/decisions.json` if they are away). A same-session "verification" is not one.
- Model switching: the tier→model mapping lives in `flywheel/config.json` (codex
  entries). When a task belongs to a tier mapped to a different model, tell the human
  which model to switch to, quoting config.json — never a model name from memory.
- State honestly in reports what degraded mode cost: no context isolation, no
  parallelism, verification only as independent as the human made it.

## Hard rules (point-of-use duplicates — keep identical to INDEX.md)
- HR1. Never Read a file listed in `flywheel/FACTS.md` §Big files (or any file > 200 KB)
  wholesale — slice via grep/jq/python.
- HR2. Model names / effort values / API params come from `flywheel/config.json` +
  `flywheel/FACTS.md` only. Missing → write `Pending verification`, never invent.
- HR3. No agent declares its own work complete — fresh-session Template 4 verdict.
- HR4. Ask-vs-act is governed by `flywheel/AUTONOMY.md`; its level-invariant rows bind
  at every autonomy level.
<!-- flywheel:end -->
